ii, domestici, and scholares present at Rome to retain a subsistence-level stipend for the sake of tradition, implying that they had ceased to hold anything beyond an honorary function." the Gothic court\'s annual income of 45,000 solidi may have supported 3000-5000 administrators.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2014, 'temperature': 0.2})
